---
import HairlineFigure from "./HairlineFigure.astro";
import SystemMap from "./diagrams/SystemMap.astro";
---

<div class="landing">
  <section class="audience" aria-label="Who TriageLab is for">
    <p class="overline">Who it&rsquo;s for</p>
    <p class="audience-lead">
      Platform, SRE, and support engineers who see the same technical tickets
      week after week (timeouts, misconfigurations, failed deploys) and want
      every answer backed by evidence, not just a confident reply.
    </p>
    <ul class="chips">
      <li>On-call &amp; platform teams</li>
      <li>Support engineering</li>
      <li>Small teams on Kubernetes</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="how-a-case-moves">
    <p class="overline">The workflow</p>
    <h2>How a case moves</h2>
    <ol class="pipeline">
      <li class="stage">
        <HairlineFigure
          name="sieve"
          label="A stack of test sieves; the top one rises clear of the stack"
        />
        <p class="stage-num">01</p>
        <h3>Route</h3>
        <p>
          Ticket tags and labels select a procedure, which sets the
          checklist, clarification policy, agent, and sandbox template for
          the case.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="stage">
        <HairlineFigure
          name="query"
          label="A question mark built as a solid, its dot a loose ball"
        />
        <p class="stage-num">02</p>
        <h3>Classify</h3>
        <p>
          The procedure&rsquo;s checklist names the facts and files the case
          needs. Facts found in the ticket are sanitized into evidence, and
          anything missing becomes a clarification question.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="stage">
        <HairlineFigure
          name="padlock"
          label="A padlock whose shackle springs open"
        />
        <p class="stage-num">03</p>
        <h3>Approve</h3>
        <p>
          A person approves the exact sanitized facts, file hashes, agent,
          and limits. The approval expires quickly and is checked again at
          launch.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="stage">
        <HairlineFigure
          name="terminal"
          label="A terminal window; lines lift off the screen under the pointer"
        />
        <p class="stage-num">04</p>
        <h3>Investigate</h3>
        <p>
          Each run gets its own disposable gVisor or microVM sandbox with
          egress denied. A kagent investigator runs the experiments, and
          TriageLab records every process directly from the sandbox.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="stage">
        <HairlineFigure
          name="format"
          label="A formatter squaring crooked lines to their indents"
        />
        <p class="stage-num">05</p>
        <h3>Report</h3>
        <p>
          JSON and Markdown reports keep what was observed separate from the
          model&rsquo;s hypothesis. A reviewed summary can go back to the
          ticket with the full evidence trail.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="pipeline-note">
      No untrusted ticket content reaches the sandbox until a person has seen
      exactly what will run. Once a run starts, upstream isolation and egress
      policy enforce the hard limits, not the prompt.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="where-the-work-runs">
    <p class="overline">Under the hood</p>
    <h2>Where the work runs</h2>
    <SystemMap />
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="why-triagelab">
    <p class="overline">Why TriageLab</p>
    <h2>Evidence you can defend</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Evidence, not answers</h3>
        <p>
          Process state, exit codes, and output come straight from the
          sandbox, never from the model&rsquo;s say-so. Any explanation of
          the cause is labeled as a hypothesis.
        </p>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/TriageLab/articles/evidence-not-answers/"
          >Read the article &rarr;</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Sandboxed by default</h3>
        <p>
          Every run uses a disposable gVisor or microVM sandbox. Egress is
          denied by default, and watchdogs enforce time and size limits.
          kagent runs the investigator; Agent Substrate provides the
          isolation.
        </p>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/TriageLab/reference/architecture/"
          >Architecture &rarr;</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>A human approves every run</h3>
        <p>
          Approval covers the exact evidence and run settings. It expires
          quickly and is checked again at launch, so an outdated plan cannot
          start.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <h3>Your tracker stays the record</h3>
        <p>
          Zendesk, GitHub, and Linear tickets enter the same workflow through
          policy-checked sources. The conversation stays in your tracker.
        </p>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/TriageLab/guides/tickets-zendesk/"
          >Ticket guides &rarr;</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="is-it-for-you">
    <p class="overline">Honest fit</p>
    <h2>Is it for you?</h2>
    <div class="fit">
      <div class="fit-card">
        <h3>A good fit today</h3>
        <ul class="fit-list yes">
          <li>
            Your small team handles repetitive technical tickets: timeouts,
            misconfigurations, failed deploys.
          </li>
          <li>
            You already run Kubernetes and can dedicate a cluster to
            TriageLab.
          </li>
          <li>
            You want AI help that shows its work, with every claim traced to
            a recorded process.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="fit-card not">
        <h3>Not yet</h3>
        <ul class="fit-list no">
          <li>
            It is an early, single-user pilot, not a production support
            platform.
          </li>
          <li>
            The workflow is general, but every source currently uses the same
            Python 3.12 timeout procedure.
          </li>
          <li>There is no database, operator, or multi-tenant deployment.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-label="Get started">
    <div class="cta-copy">
      <h2>Start with the included example</h2>
      <p>
        The quickstart runs a full investigation of a small Python
        application with a timeout configuration error: it reproduces the
        error, finds the units mismatch, and verifies the fix.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a class="cta-btn" href="/TriageLab/start/quickstart/"
        >Run the quickstart</a
      >
      <a class="cta-btn ghost" href="/TriageLab/reference/cli/"
        >Browse the CLI reference</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  import {
    loupe,
    sieve,
    query,
    padlock,
    terminal,
    format,
  } from "@lucasmarkes/hairline";

  const figures = { loupe, sieve, query, padlock, terminal, format };

  for (const el of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-hairline]")) {
    const draw = figures[el.dataset.hairline as keyof typeof figures];
    if (!draw) continue;
    const intensity = Number.parseFloat(el.dataset.intensity ?? "");
    draw(el, {
      play: el.dataset.play === "true",
      intensity: Number.isFinite(intensity) ? intensity : undefined,
      label: el.getAttribute("aria-label") ?? undefined,
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* --- Page rhythm ------------------------------------------------ */

  .landing {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-sans);
  }

  .section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.875rem;
  }

  .landing h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.9rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--bondren-ink);
  }

  .landing h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-sans);
    color: var(--bondren-ink);
  }

  .landing p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Mono overline with a short drafter's rule in the accent. */
  .overline {
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bondren-accent);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.625rem;
  }
  .overline::before {
    content: "";
    width: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--bondren-accent);
  }

  /* --- Audience band ---------------------------------------------- */

  .audience {
    background: var(--bondren-plate);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-line-frame);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--bondren-accent);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-plate);
    padding: 1.375rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .audience-lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-2);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .chips {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .chips li {
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-muted);
    background: var(--bondren-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-line-frame);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius-sm);
    padding: 0.1875rem 0.5625rem;
  }

  /* --- Pipeline ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .pipeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.875rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(11.5rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .stage {
    background: var(--bondren-plate);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-line-frame);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--bondren-rule-cut);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-plate);
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }
  .stage .hairline-figure {
    --hairline-plate: var(--bondren-plate);
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
    max-width: 14rem;
  }
  .stage-num {
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--bondren-accent);
  }
  .stage p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-muted);
  }
  .pipeline-note {
    margin-top: 0.875rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    background: var(--bondren-well);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--bondren-rule-cut);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-2);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  /* --- Feature cards ----------------------------------------------- */

  .features {
    margin-top: 0.875rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .feature {
    background: var(--bondren-plate);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-line-frame);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-plate);
    padding: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.625rem;
  }
  .feature p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-muted);
    flex-grow: 1;
  }
  .feature-link {
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--bondren-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    width: fit-content;
  }
  .feature-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* --- Fit columns -------------------------------------------------- */

  .fit {
    margin-top: 0.875rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .fit-card {
    background: var(--bondren-plate);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-line-frame);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-plate);
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }
  .fit-card.not {
    background: var(--bondren-well);
    border-color: var(--bondren-line-frame);
  }
  .fit-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.875rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.625rem;
  }
  .fit-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.375rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--bondren-ink-2);
  }
  .fit-list li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
  }
  .fit-list.yes li::before {
    content: "+";
    color: var(--bondren-success);
  }
  .fit-list.no li::before {
    content: "\2013";
    color: var(--bondren-rule-cut);
  }

  /* --- Closing CTA band --------------------------------------------- */

  .cta-band {
    background: var(--bondren-ink);
    color: var(--bondren-paper);
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-pop);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .cta-copy {
    max-width: 44ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.625rem;
  }
  .cta-band h2 {
    color: var(--bondren-paper);
  }
  .cta-band p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--bondren-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }
  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .cta-btn {
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    padding: 0.6875rem 1.125rem;
    background: var(--bondren-accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--bondren-accent);
    color: var(--bondren-paper);
  }
  .cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--bondren-accent-press);
    border-color: var(--bondren-accent-press);
  }
  .cta-btn.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--bondren-paper) 45%, transparent);
    color: var(--bondren-paper);
  }
  .cta-btn.ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--bondren-paper);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bondren-paper) 10%, transparent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    .landing {
      gap: 2.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  /* Starlight renders the hero from frontmatter and wraps this component's
     markup in .sl-markdown-content, so those elements need global rules.
     This stylesheet is bundled only on pages that use LandingSections. */

  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vmin, 3.5rem);
  }
  .hero > .hero-html {
    order: 2;
    width: min(100%, 24rem);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .hero .tagline {
    color: var(--bondren-ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .hero-accent {
    color: var(--bondren-accent);
  }

  /* Square the pill-shaped action buttons to the Bondren radius. */
  .hero .sl-link-button {
    border-radius: var(--bondren-radius);
    font-family: var(--bondren-font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .hero .sl-link-button.secondary {
    border-color: var(--bondren-line-frame);
  }
  .hero .sl-link-button.minimal {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  /* Prose on the landing page keeps a reading measure while the designed
     sections span the full splash width. */
  .sl-markdown-content > :not(.landing) {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  /* Isometric line figures: graphite ink on the surface they sit on. The
     Bondren tokens swap automatically in dark mode. */
  .hairline-figure,
  .hairline-hero {
    --hairline-plate: var(--bondren-paper);
    --hairline-hi: var(--bondren-ink);
    --hairline-edge: var(--bondren-ink-2);
    --hairline-mid: var(--bondren-ink-muted);
    --hairline-lo: var(--bondren-line-object);
    --hairline-stroke: 1.15;
  }
  .hairline-hero {
    width: 100%;
  }
</style>
